# Nechto — agent context

Art-space platform for the Belarus market. Monorepo scaffold; product is early MVP.

## Stack

- `apps/web` — Next.js 15 (App Router) + Tailwind CSS 4 + TypeScript + next-intl (ru default, en)
- `apps/api` — NestJS 11 + TypeScript (`module`/`moduleResolution`: `nodenext`) + Prisma + Zod env
- PostgreSQL 16 via Docker Compose (`prisma migrate deploy` on API start)
- Local run: `docker compose up --build`
- Shared TS: `tsconfig.base.json` (strict); no deprecated `baseUrl` / `moduleResolution: node`

## Layout

```
apps/web   # frontend (app/[locale], messages/, i18n/, lib/env.ts)
apps/api   # backend API (prisma/, config/env.ts)
docker-compose.yml
tsconfig.base.json
```

## Agent conventions

- Keep changes scoped; no drive-by refactors
- Prefer TypeScript everywhere (configs included when practical)
- Do not add Kubernetes / LangChain / payments until product needs them
- Verify with `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run format:check` when touching shared tooling or many files
- Format with Prettier (`prettier.config.mjs`); do not fight it with manual style diffs
- Auth uses JWT httpOnly cookies + `JwtAuthGuard`; never store passwords in plaintext
- File uploads go through `StorageService` (local disk in dev); do not write ad-hoc disk/S3 calls in feature modules
- Match IDE TypeScript strictness when relevant (CSS side-effect imports need `*.css` module declarations)
- Comments: English only (see `english-comments` rule)
- UI copy: Russian + English via next-intl (see `i18n-bilingual` rule)
- Commits: English Conventional Commits (see `conventional-commits` rule)
- Tests: Jest for API, Playwright for UI; cover new behavior (see `testing` rule)
